  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "DeepSeek Harness Status Hub",
      "text": "A browser-side DeepSeek Harness plugin that adds a status hub to the sidebar. It uses the shipped Web UI extension points and reads existing Host services without introducing another server."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "Install the prebuilt GitHub Release:\n\n```powershell\ndsh plugin --profile web add https://github.com/HUSTforever/dsh-status-hub/releases/download/v0.1.0/dsh-status-hub-0.1.0.tgz\n```\n\nRestart `dsh web`, then use the Status Hub icon in the sidebar footer.\n\nAfter an npm release is available, `dsh plugin --profile web add dsh-status-hub` is equivalent."
    },
    {
      "section": "Views",
      "text": "- Overview: connection, active sessions, plugins, MCP servers, and skills.\n- Sessions: live session list with running state and navigation.\n- MCP: configured `@deepseek-ai/dsh-mcp-client` Loader entries and lifecycle state.\n- Skills: the `skills/list` catalog for the currently selected session.\n- Plugins: the read-only global Loader inventory with search and failure state."
    },
    {
      "section": "Local development",
      "text": "```powershell\npnpm install\npnpm run build\ndsh plugin --profile web add .\ndsh --profile web --no-open --port 3081\n\nOpen the authenticated local URL printed by `dsh`. The profile dependency remains linked to this checkout, so rebuild and restart after changing the client bundle."
    },
    {
      "section": "Compatibility",
      "text": "The package follows the documented dual-face plugin contract: an empty Host `apply()` entry, a `dsh.bundle` profile layer, a `dsh.client` Web declaration, an exported `./client` bundle, and slot registration through `ctx.slots.inject()`. Its development dependencies target the `0.1.2-rc.1` Web packages installed with the current local Harness distribution."
    },
    {
      "section": "Compatibility",
      "text": "MCP status is Loader-level status. Harness currently exposes MCP tools through the tool registry but does not expose a dedicated browser Remote for per-server health, so this view reports configuration and Fiber lifecycle without probing external servers."
    },
    {
      "section": "Distribution",
      "text": "`pnpm pack` creates a prebuilt tarball that users can install without approving a source-build script:\n\n```powershell\ndsh plugin --profile web add ./dsh-status-hub-0.1.0.tgz\n```\n\nFor GitHub source installs, the `prepare` script builds `lib/`; pnpm 10 and newer require users to approve that install-time build. Publishing the prebuilt package to npm provides the simplest installation path.\n\nSee [MARKETPLACE.md](./MARKETPLACE.md) for the GitHub and `awesome-dsh-plugin` submission checklist."
    }
  ],
